{
    "_comment": [
        "stablecoins: tokens pinned to $1.",
        "feeds: token -> Chainlink-compatible aggregator for its USD price.",
        "feedDecimals: per-feed scale override, for aggregators that do not expose decimals().",
        "defaultFeedDecimals: fallback scale per network when decimals() reverts and no override is set.",
        "  18 preserves this indexer's historical behaviour. Chainlink USD aggregators are",
        "  conventionally 8 - verify each feed and pin it in feedDecimals rather than relying on this.",
        "NOTE: collateral tokens generally do NOT need an entry here. The indexer reads each",
        "market's own Morpho oracle and derives the collateral's USD price from the loan asset's,",
        "so anchoring loan assets (usually stablecoins) is enough.",
        "ETHEREUM/BASE: every address below was read back from chain - ERC20 symbol()/decimals()",
        "for tokens, aggregator description()/decimals() for feeds. Their Chainlink feeds report",
        "8 decimals, so both the per-feed overrides and defaultFeedDecimals are 8 on those two",
        "networks (18 elsewhere, preserving the older networks' behaviour). WETH and WBTC/cbBTC",
        "get direct feeds because they are loan assets on Ethereum/Base, not only collateral."
    ],
